  "body": "With the latest switch to the Infra errors on null characters in input stream are reported twice:\r\n1. In \"12.2.2.5 Preprocessing the input stream\" section:\r\n\r\n> Any occurrences of surrogates, noncharacters, or controls other than ASCII whitespace are parse errors.\r\n\r\nAnd `0x00` is a C0 control.\r\n\r\n2. Tokenizer states have dedicated branches for `NULL` that report error as well.\r\n\r\nThe obvious solution is to remove error reporting in tokenizer states, however nulls have special treatment: they are either replaced or completely ignored, whereas other controls are kept as is. Therefore, semantically it will be better to change error reporting in input stream, e.g.:\r\n\r\n>  Any occurrences of surrogates, noncharacters, or controls other than ASCII whitespace and 0x00 NULL are parse errors.\r\n",
